        "notes": "The block's own claim is an EQUIVALENCE ('instantiating BarEvenKernel is equivalent to clearing all four gates simultaneously' / 'requires clearing all four mass-side gates simultaneously'), and only the forward half had Lean. The three lifting lemmas each return the class field their type restates -- the accessor idiom (Group.mul_assoc), one direction of the equivalence, not a derivation. The converse was never stated. Added barEvenKernel_iff / massSideKernel_iff, so the equivalence the .md asserts is now in the Lean and the accessors are one half of it. RETRACTION of a hypothesis of mine: I suspected the theorem->def conversion in 7e9230d39a9 ('remediate 310 lean vacuity findings', 82 conversions across 69 files) had HIDDEN bar_even_kernel_implies_q_one_shadow from the detector, on the evidence that its two neighbours have vacuity-ledger entries and it has none. Measured: FALSE. A fresh lean-vacuity-axiom-audit run flags it at L122 as proof-no-self-assuming-projection despite being a def; it is absent from the ledger because it is EXEMPT ('canonical 3b placeholder projection (tracked; derivation pending)'), and exempt findings get no ledger entry. The kind change does not evade the detector. Bean qou-z9ws."
