        "notes": "Re-verified after adding barEvenKernelAtIntendedPoint + barEvenKernel_nonempty. The 2026-08-31 pass STANDS and this entry does not revise it: its finding -- that the block claims an EQUIVALENCE, that the three lifting lemmas are the accessor idiom giving one direction, and that barEvenKernel_iff supplies the other -- is still exactly what the Lean says. Re-adjudicated only because the .lean hash drifted (b4470b4cb092 -> aef8d4c64cbc); nothing in the prior verdict is withdrawn. What this change adds is orthogonal to the equivalence and to proof-statement-integrity: an ACCEPTANCE witness. The file proved the gate can reject (bar_even_kernel_reject_wrong_c2_shadow) and never that it can accept, and those are not the same evidence. Under the qou-z9ws inhabitation discriminator a projection is the legitimate accessor idiom ONLY when something builds the bundle; the witness existed but lived in docs/audits/2026-08-30-gate-classes-admit-zero.lean, which has no imports and is imported by nothing (these classes are content-block siblings, not library modules), so it was unreachable from the class it certifies. Reproduced at the class as a def, not an instance. Verified lean-direct exit 0 with -DautoImplicit=false -s 65536. NOT claimed: the three projections are still projections and the detector still flags them -- correctly; what changed is that their legitimacy is now checkable from this file rather than from an unimported probe."
